TIP:  Of course Sting wrote and made it famous but I've patterned the one here after Eva's version as it's one of the most sublime things I've ever heard.  Even more poignant as she must have known by this point she didn't have long to live when she sang it.  You can still play along with Sting's original but you'll have to capo 7 and the verses are a little different.  Sting plays a verse that Eva does not and coming out of the instrumental bridge he goes to the final verse while Eva does a reprise. 


